Body:
Another vote for this. I think it should allow custom modes/agents in config that can be activated via `session/set_mode`, that way you can switch in the same session. But also, adding a prompt in the config would be worthwhile as well. For example... 

```jsonc
{
  "agent": {
    "reviewer": {
      "mode": "primary",
      "prompt": "You are in review mode. You are read-only. Report findings using the annotation tool.",
      "tools": {
        "read": true,
        "grep": true,
        "glob": true,
        "edit": false,
        "write": false,
        "bash": false
      },
      "mcp": {
        // Only these MCP server tools are visible to the model in this mode
        "annotation-server": true,
        "file-editor-server": false
      }
    },
    "scoped-editor": {
      "mode": "primary",
      "prompt": "Use the file_edit MCP tool to make changes. If rejected, move on.",
      "tools": {
        "edit": false,
        "write": false
      },
      "mcp": {
        "file-editor-server": true,
        "annotation-server": false
      }
    }
  }
}
```

Then an ACP client sends `session/set_mode` with `{"modeId": "reviewer"}` and the model's visible tools and system prompt switch accordingly, so it's more knowledgeable as to what happened in the switch.

